  "Particles, ribbons, lights, modern shader combiners and camera animation are dropped (see the report).",
  "Replaces the model for every display that uses it; native skin names are reused for the modern skins.",
  "Character pilot (W11): TBC-era character/bloodelf/male/bloodelfmale.m2 (FileDataID 117170, byte-identical in Forever and Retail; Retail is read because Forever has the eye-glow BLP offline) -> native Character/BloodElf/Male/BloodElfMale.m2. Every geoset the native character logic knows is kept (hair 1-17, facial 102-110, gloves, boots, ears, sleeves, kneepads, chest, pants, tabard, robe, cloaks 1501-1506) plus eye glow 1702; dropped: 1104, cloaks 1507-1510 (modern customization textures 15-18), DK eye glow 1703, belt 1802. Body/hair/cape stay replaceable (types 1/6/2) for the game's compositor and CharSections."
 ]
